<title>POLAND: All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</title>
<headline>All Polish minimum T-bill prices fall at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>All Polish minimum T-bill prices fell at today's primary auction on total demand of 334 million zlotys against a one billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold a total of 333 million zlotys worth of the bills.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week 39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price     --     95.20    90.79     --	82.90</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.24)  (90.85)    --     (83.16)</p>
<p>   new max price     --     95.28    90.88     --	83.40</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)     --    (95.35)  (90.89)    --     (83.40)</p>
<p>   offer		 --     300.0    200.0     --	500.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded     --	85.0     26.4     --	222.6</p>
<p>   bids accepted     --	84.0     26.4     --	222.6</p>
<p>   next auction	--     300.0    200.0     --	500.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
